on":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Anthony Lapointe","displayName":"Anthony Lapointe","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Drake Batherson has 3 goals and an assist in the Senators' 7-4 victory over the Rangers","description":"— Drake Batherson had three goals and an assist and the Ottawa Senators outscored the New York Rangers 7-4 on Saturday night.","story":"OTTAWA, Ontario -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4271734/drake-batherson\">Drake Batherson</a> had three goals and an assist and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/ott/ottawa-senators\">Ottawa Senators</a> outscored the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nyr/new-york-rangers\">New York Rangers</a> 7-4 on Saturday night.\n\n\r\n              Jake Sanderson’s first of the season proved to be the winner and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3149829/michael-amadio\">Michael Amadio</a> added an empty-netter. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697384/tim-stutzle\">Tim Stutzle</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565228/dylan-cozens\">Dylan Cozens</a> also scored and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3115546/jonas-johansson\">Jonas Johansson</a> stopped 24 shots in his Ottawa debut.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697468/will-cuylle\">Will Cuylle</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2590852/jt-miller\">J.T. Miller</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697382/alexis-lafreniere\">Alexis Lafreniere</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4587588/pavel-dorofeyev\">Pavel Dorofeyev</a> scored for the Rangers. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697705/dylan-garand\">Dylan Garand</a> made 17 saves.\n\n\r\n              Sanderson’s first of the season was a big one. Garand made an initial save on <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697411/ridly-greig\">Ridly Greig</a>, and Sanderson buried the rebound to make it 5-3. \n\n\r\n              The Rangers got back within one on Dorofeyev's snap shot with 4:28 remaining.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Rangers: Host Los Angeles on Monday night.\n\n\r\n              Senators: At Vegas on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-25T02:15:48Z"}}